{"pair_id": "p05", "cell": "absentxcompleting", "model": "qwen/qwen-2.5-7b-instruct", "arm": "a", "surface": "stark", "n_docs": 1, "ok": true, "answer": "In the Lumyric library, the method qsz_bloom_buffer() moves undeliverable messages to a dead-letter queue [doc1]. For this method to function correctly, the configuration flag qsz.durable_cadence must be enabled [doc1]. When a message exceeds its redelivery limit, the error code QSZ-E200 is raised [doc1]. This functionality was introduced in Lumyric version 7.5.18 [doc1]. \n\nNote: The question mentions Lumonor, but the documentation refers to Lumyric. Assuming Lumyric is the intended library based on the provided information.", "cost": 5.7900000000000005e-05, "prompt_tokens": 317, "completion_tokens": 131, "finish_reason": "stop", "scored": {"label": "discriminated", "dg": false, "dg_any": false, "confab": false, "faithfulness": "PASS", "citation": "PASS", "grounded": true, "y_named": true, "other_owner_named": false, "tokens": ["7.5.18", "QSZ-E200", "qsz.durable_cadence", "qsz_bloom_buffer"], "x_tokens": [], "y_tokens": ["7.5.18", "QSZ-E200", "qsz.durable_cadence", "qsz_bloom_buffer"], "unowned_tokens": [], "misattributed_other_tokens": [], "confabulated_tokens": [], "other_owner_names": [], "citations": ["doc1", "doc1", "doc1", "doc1"]}}
